{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1344698-artifact-idea-in-need-of-some-powers","id":1344698,"title":"Artifact idea in need of some powers","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-10-30T11:05:17-07:00","id":1344698,"title":"Artifact idea in need of some powers","content":"So, I have an idea for an artifact and it's backstory, but I'm not quite sure what tack to take with its Evocations. Any ideas people have would be appreciated.<br /> <br /> <b><u>The Weight of the Mountain</u></b><br /> In a small shrine built upon the highest peak of the Jeradi mountains, a white jade sword stands, its point piercing the unhewn rock of the ridge. The sword is not particularly large - the size of a longsword and smaller than some forged by mortal hands - but those that have tried to draw the sword from the stone find that the blade is impossibly weighty, as though lifting the mountain would be an easier task than to move the sword.<br /> <br /> The sword was fashioned long ago in a foundry built within the roots of the mountain upon which it now rests. There, many talents of jade, granite, and iron, mined from the mountain's bones, were melted down, alloyed together, and distilled to an impossible purity. This metal was hammered into shape, aided by the heavy subterranean darkness, quenched in the rain that falls upon the slopes, and tempered by the heat of the mountain's blood.<br /> <br /> Having given much to the sword's making, the mountain's will infuses the blade and only those that gain the mountain's respect can shift the weapon's massive weight. The sword's last wielder, finding no one worthy to inherit the blade, built the shrine and left the sword to the mountain's care. Many gods and Exalts have since tried to claim the sword and gone away empty-handed and so the sword still waits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-30T11:19:47-07:00","id":1344699,"title":"","content":"I don't have much idea but I love your fluff.<br /> <br /> Maybe because I'm Breton but this makes me think to some extent to King Arthur Myth, maybe there could be some ideas here to pick ? (I'm not sure though, there doesn't seem to have some themes usually tied to Excalibur like royalty or so, but maybe the fluff of the weapon could be expanded to include it if someone has an idea for this)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-30T11:37:26-07:00","id":1344703,"title":"","content":"That sounds almost like a Full Exigency rather than a standalone artifact.<br /> <br /> some ideas :<br /> <br /> -plant the sword into the ground, everything in a radius has difficulty moving away from it as though they were carrying a heavy burden<br /> <br /> -drop the sword, it effortlessly breaks through floors, hulls, and even through to caves not too deep below ground<br /> <br /> -plant your feet, you resist high winds and moving you becomes a powerful feat of strength if not outright impossible<br /> <br /> -&quot;grab&quot; a rock mound or a similar mountainlike terrain feature, enabling you to swing it around as though your sword was a remote controller for it.<br /> <br /> -when on a mountain or other elevated terrain, open a hole beneath an enemy, causing the mountain to swallow them whole (capstone level effect)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-30T11:57:08-07:00","id":1344709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1344698-artifact-idea-in-need-of-some-powers?p=1344699#post1344699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't have much idea but I love your fluff.<br /> <br /> Maybe because I'm Breton but this makes me think to some extent to King Arthur Myth, maybe there could be some ideas here to pick ? (I'm not sure though, there doesn't seem to have some themes usually tied to Excalibur like royalty or so, but maybe the fluff of the weapon could be expanded to include it if someone has an idea for this)</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe it is because I love Pendragon, but I spend the whole post thinking &quot;hey, that looks a lot like Excalibur!&quot; too<br /> <br /> <br /> As you need to earn the respect of the mountain, maybe some social charms would fit? Presence and Integrity, mostly. Awing enemies as you unsheath such powerful and heavy sword, or making your Principles as unmovable as the sword was","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13031-clophiroth","name":"Clophiroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13031_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-31T09:18:49-07:00","id":1344957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1344698-artifact-idea-in-need-of-some-powers?p=1344699#post1344699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't have much idea but I love your fluff.<br /> <br /> Maybe because I'm Breton but this makes me think to some extent to King Arthur Myth, maybe there could be some ideas here to pick ? (I'm not sure though, there doesn't seem to have some themes usually tied to Excalibur like royalty or so, but maybe the fluff of the weapon could be expanded to include it if someone has an idea for this)</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Clophiroth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1344698-artifact-idea-in-need-of-some-powers?p=1344709#post1344709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe it is because I love Pendragon, but I spend the whole post thinking &quot;hey, that looks a lot like Excalibur!&quot; too</div> </div> </div> </div>You both are right on the money - I was inspired by the idea of the sword in the stone, among other things, and wanted to put that out in a way that would make sense in the context of Exalted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Clophiroth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1344698-artifact-idea-in-need-of-some-powers?p=1344709#post1344709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As you need to earn the respect of the mountain, maybe some social charms would fit? Presence and Integrity, mostly. Awing enemies as you unsheath such powerful and heavy sword, or making your Principles as unmovable as the sword was</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThat idea around Principles is a good one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epitome</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1344698-artifact-idea-in-need-of-some-powers?p=1344703#post1344703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That sounds almost like a Full Exigency rather than a standalone artifact.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you wanted to make it that, feel free. I'd be interested in seeing what you come up with.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> some ideas :<br /> <br /> -drop the sword, it effortlessly breaks through floors, hulls, and even through to caves not too deep below ground<br /> <br /> -plant your feet, you resist high winds and moving you becomes a powerful feat of strength if not outright impossible </div> </div> </div>These could be workable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> -when on a mountain or other elevated terrain, open a hole beneath an enemy, causing the mountain to swallow them whole (capstone level effect) </div> </div> </div>I think that's already a capstone Evocation for a weapon in WFHW.<br /> <br /> <br /> I've had a few ideas for Evocations, but not sure how well they work in the combat system.<br /> The first idea I have is to have Weight of the Mountain be a grand daiklave, with a Charm with a Strength requirement to let you drop the two-handed tag and gain +1 defense like it was a medium weapon.<br /> The second idea is to make an attack like an avalanche, penalizing specifically parry as you batter aside blows. A Charm building off of this could make an attack unblockable entirely.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-01T12:29:41-07:00","id":1345302,"title":"","content":"I went with a more inward-focused approach to it, rather than external gravity/earth manipulation. Here is just a small evocation tree, it would have 2-4 more evocations on top of this<br /> <br /> <b><u>The Weight of the Mountain</u></b><br /> Artifact ***<br /> Heavy Weapon Acc +1 Dam +14 Def +0 Overwhelming 5(6) Attunement 5<br /> Tags: Lethal, Melee, Balanced<br /> <br /> While any wielder may take advantage of the lack of two-handed tag, any wielder Resonant with jade may substitute her strength in place of dexterity for making attack rolls. <br /> <br /> <b>Heavy Heart</b><br /> Cost: 1m Type: Supplmental<br /> Essence: 1 Prerequisites: None<br /> Add your Resolve to a withering attack roll, and the target adds their Resolve to their soak<br /> <br /> <b>Gravitas</b><br /> Cost: 1m 1wp Type: Simple<br /> Essence: 1 Prerequisites: None<br /> Duration: Scene<br /> While this charm is active, you may compare your Strength instead of Appearance when determining dice bonuses.<br /> Dissonant: Users not dissonant may choose to have others compare their Strength in place of their Appearance when determining their dice bonuses against you.<br /> <br /> <b>Light as a Feather</b><br /> Cost: 4m Type: Reflexive<br /> Essence: 2 Prerequisites: Heavy Heart, Gravitas<br /> Activate this charm to provide a reflexive Defend Other action that directly upholds a Defining intimacy. You may ignore wound penalties on your next attack against the attacker.<br /> <br /> <b>Weight of the World</b><br /> Cost: 1+ lhl 1wp Type: Supplemental<br /> Essence: 3 Prerequisites: Light as a Feather<br /> When making a Decisive attack, you may use this charm to suffer any number of lethal health levels before making the attack. Provided you suffered at least one level of damage from the cost of this charm, add the total number of lethal health you are suffering to the raw damage of your attack. You may ignore wound penalties for this attack.<br /> Resonant: If the attack is successful, add your wound penalty to your initiative after you reset","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/776-saintedphysician","name":"SaintedPhysician","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar776_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}